{title: The Hallelujah Side}
{key: G}
{x_theme: heaven, praise, grace-mercy, salvation}
{x_source: chrd:the_hallelujah_side.chrd}

{comment: Chorus}
[G]Oh,  [C]glory be to Jesus, let the [G]hallelujahs roll;
[G]Help me ring the Savior's praises far and [D]wide,
[G]For I've opened up tow'rd Hea-ven all the [C]windows of my soul,
[G]And I'm living on the [D]hallelujah [G]side.

{comment: Verse 1}
[G]Once a sinner far from Jesus,
I was [C]perishing with [G]cold,
But the blessed Savior heard me when I [D]cried;
Then He threw His robe around me,
[G]And He [C]led me to His [G]fold,
And I'm living on the [D]hallelujah [G]side.

{comment: Verse 2}
[G]Tho' the world may sweep around me
With her [C]dazzle and her [G]dreams,
Yet I envy not her vanities and [D]pride,
For my soul looks up to heaven,
[G]Where the [C]golden sunlight [G]gleams,
And I'm living on the [D]hallelujah [G]side.

{comment: Verse 3}
[G]Not for all earth's golden millions
Would I [C]leave this precious [G]place,
Tho' the tempter to persuade me oft has [D]tried,
For I'm safe in God's pavilion,
[G]Happy in [C]His love and [G]grace,
And I'm living on the [D]hallelujah [G]side.

{comment: Verse 4}
[G]Here the sun is always shining,
Here the [C]sky is always [G]bright;
'Tis no place for gloomy Christians to a[D]bide,
For my soul is filled with music
[G]And my [C]heart with great [G]delight,
And I'm living on the [D]hallelujah [G]side.

{comment: Verse 5}
[G]And upon the streets of glory,
When we [C]reach the other [G]shore,
And have safely crossed the Jordan's rolling [D]tide,
You will find me shouting "Glory"
[G]Just out[C]side my mansion [G]door
Where I'm living on the [D]hallelujah [G]side.
